## 2. Layer Your Bedding for Warmth and Texture

One flat bedspread makes a room look like a hotel. Layered bedding makes it feel lived-in and cozy. Think of it like dressing the bed the way you'd dress for a cold morning — in layers.

[![Layered kids bedding with chunky knit blanket, throw pillows, and a patterned duvet]({{ site.baseurl }}/assets/images/home-decor/layered-kids-bedding.jpg)](https://pin.it/XXXXXXX)

**A simple layering formula:**
1. Start with a fitted sheet in a solid color
2. Add a duvet or comforter in a soft pattern (stars, animals, simple stripes)
3. Fold a textured throw blanket at the foot of the bed
4. Toss in 2–3 throw pillows in mix-and-match sizes

**Material tip:** For kids under 8, go with cotton or cotton-blend — it's easy to wash and gentle on skin. Avoid heavy wool or synthetic fills that trap heat.

| Material | Warmth Level | Washability | Cost |
|---|---|---|---|
| Cotton | Medium | Easy | $25–$60 |
| Microfiber | Medium-High | Easy | $20–$45 |
| Chunky knit throw | High | Hand-wash | $30–$70 |
| Faux fur throw | High | Dry clean | $25–$55 |

