## 4. Use Warm, Soft Lighting (Not Overhead Lights)

Overhead lighting kills cozy. Warm, low lighting at different heights is what makes a room feel like a hug. Think of how coffee shops do it — no one sits under a fluorescent tube.

[![Warm fairy lights and a small bedside lamp creating soft glow in a kids room at night]({{ site.baseurl }}/assets/images/home-decor/warm-kids-room-lighting.jpg)](https://pin.it/XXXXXXX)

**Lighting layers to use:**

### H3: Ambient (Background) Light
- Plug-in pendant lamp or a floor lamp in the corner
- Use bulbs with warm color temperature: 2700K–3000K

### H3: Accent Light
- Fairy lights along the headboard, around a mirror, or in a canopy
- LED strip lights behind a bookshelf (low-profile, fun glow)

### H3: Task Light
- A clip-on or small bedside lamp for reading
- Rechargeable options are great — no cord clutter

| Light Type | Cost | Where to Buy |
|---|---|---|
| Fairy lights (USB) | $8–$20 | Amazon, Target |
| Plug-in pendant | $25–$60 | Wayfair, IKEA |
| Clip-on reading light | $12–$30 | Amazon |
| Smart bulb (dimmable) | $10–$20/bulb | Amazon, Home Depot |

**Pro tip:** Put a smart bulb in the main fixture and connect it to Alexa or Google Home. Kids love telling a device to dim the lights for bedtime.

