## 5. Add a Soft Area Rug

Hard floors feel cold and impersonal. A large, soft rug grounds the room and makes the whole space feel warmer — literally and visually.

[![A large round cream rug with a kids low bed and wooden toys on top in a Scandinavian kids room]({{ site.baseurl }}/assets/images/home-decor/soft-area-rug-kids-room.jpg)](https://pin.it/XXXXXXX)

**Sizing guide:**

| Room Size | Rug Size |
|---|---|
| Small (9×10 ft) | 5×7 ft |
| Medium (10×12 ft) | 6×9 ft |
| Large (12×14 ft+) | 8×10 ft or 9×12 ft |

The rug should extend at least 18 inches past the sides and foot of the bed.

**Best materials for kids' rooms:**
- **Polypropylene (synthetic):** Stain-resistant, easy to clean — best for messy kids
- **Cotton flatweave:** Soft, machine washable, affordable
- **Wool:** Durable and naturally stain-resistant but pricier and harder to clean

**Where to buy:** IKEA, Rugs USA, Wayfair, Target. Budget: $50–$200 depending on size.

