## 6. Paint an Accent Wall in a Cozy Color

You don't need to repaint the whole room. One accent wall behind the bed does most of the heavy lifting and sets the entire mood of the space.

**Colors that work best for cozy kids' rooms:**

| Color | Mood | Best Age Range |
|---|---|---|
| Dusty sage green | Calm, nature-inspired | Any age |
| Warm terracotta | Earthy, bold | School-age+ |
| Soft navy | Cozy, classic | Any age |
| Blush pink | Soft, dreamy | Toddler to age 8 |
| Deep forest green | Dramatic, cozy | Age 7+ |
| Warm white/cream | Neutral, timeless | Any age |

**Paint brands to consider (USA):**
- Benjamin Moore Aura (best coverage, $75/gallon)
- Sherwin-Williams Emerald (low VOC, good for kids' rooms, $70/gallon)
- Behr Premium Plus (budget-friendly, $35–$45/gallon at Home Depot)

**Important:** Always use low-VOC or zero-VOC paint in kids' rooms. Ventilate the room for 48 hours after painting.

