## 8. Personalize With Wall Art and Name Decals

A cozy room feels like it belongs to someone. Personalization — even small touches — makes kids feel proud of their space and more connected to it.

**Low-effort personalization ideas:**
- Peel-and-stick name decals above the bed (Etsy, $10–$25)
- A gallery wall of their own drawings in simple frames
- A world map or constellation print they can explore
- A chalkboard or corkboard panel for changing decor as they grow

**Frame tip:** IKEA RIBBA frames ($3–$15) are the easiest way to build a gallery wall on a budget. Use a paper template to plan placement before hammering.

