## 9. Add a Canopy of Plants or Hanging Greenery

You don't need a garden — just one or two plants can make a kids' room feel alive, fresh, and cozy. Hanging plants especially add visual warmth without taking up any floor or shelf space.

**Best low-maintenance plants for kids' rooms:**

| Plant | Light Needed | Watering | Pet Safe? |
|---|---|---|---|
| Pothos | Low to medium | Every 1–2 weeks | No |
| Spider plant | Medium | Every 1–2 weeks | Yes |
| Rubber plant | Medium | Every 1–2 weeks | No |
| Air plants (Tillandsia) | Bright indirect | Mist weekly | Yes |
| Cactus | Bright | Monthly | Some species |

**Where to buy:** Home Depot, Trader Joe's (surprisingly affordable), Bloomscape (online, ships healthy plants).

**Safety note:** Keep hanging plants out of reach of toddlers. Choose non-toxic varieties if you have young children or pets.

