## 10. Create a Cozy Sleep Environment

All the decor in the world won't help if the room isn't actually set up for good sleep. The physical environment — temperature, light blocking, and sound — matters just as much as aesthetics.

**Sleep environment checklist:**

- **Blackout curtains:** Essential for nap time and early sunrises. IKEA MAJGULL ($25), Amazon basics ($20–$40)
- **White noise machine:** Helps kids fall and stay asleep. LectroFan or Marpac Dohm ($30–$55)
- **Room temperature:** 65–70°F is ideal for kids' sleep
- **Nightlight:** Warm amber or red-toned light is best — it doesn't disrupt melatonin. Hatch Rest ($70) or a simple amber plug-in nightlight ($10–$15)

| Item | Budget Option | Premium Option |
|---|---|---|
| Blackout curtains | Amazon ($20–$35) | Pottery Barn Kids ($80–$120) |
| White noise | Fan or phone app (free) | LectroFan ($55) |
| Nightlight | IKEA plug-in ($8) | Hatch Rest ($70) |

